250
00:11:37,430 --> 00:11:40,833
[Servo] Yes, let's put on
some old spice and go ashore.

251
00:11:40,833 --> 00:11:43,436
♪♪ [Whistling theme
to "old spice"]

252
00:11:44,571 --> 00:11:47,240
There's dead cows
in the water.

253
00:11:50,777 --> 00:11:52,545
Look there.

254
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:53,980
A tuna swallowed
an armadillo?

255
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:57,650
I've never seen anything
like that before.

256
00:11:57,650 --> 00:12:00,620
Some kind of coelacanth death
cult, or something, you know?

257
00:12:02,755 --> 00:12:05,425
Well, let's sell it
to the japanese for $60,000.

258
00:12:06,693 --> 00:12:09,963
The whole ocean bottom
must have been torn up

259
00:12:09,963 --> 00:12:13,132
[crow] Ugh. Can I wipe
on your jacket, please?

260
00:12:14,367 --> 00:12:16,669
Wow. New island got
settled very quickly.

261
00:12:16,669 --> 00:12:20,206
- And how.
- Lice for sale!
Sugars and lice!

262
00:12:26,546 --> 00:12:28,114
Looks like they were
pretty hard hit.

263
00:12:28,114 --> 00:12:30,817
- Yeah.
- Poor dopes. They appear
every hundred years

264
00:12:30,817 --> 00:12:33,186
- and get hit by a huge storm.
- Hi.

265
00:12:33,186 --> 00:12:34,887
Is there a harbormaster
we can talk to?

266
00:12:34,887 --> 00:12:36,189
[Speaking foreign language]

267
00:12:36,189 --> 00:12:38,524
- Something about a knish?
- Ooh.

268
00:12:38,524 --> 00:12:40,860
Gaelic, huh?

269
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:43,229
Doesn't sound like "welcome"
in any language.

270
00:12:43,229 --> 00:12:45,498
How do you get your shirts
so white, seamus?

271
00:12:51,204 --> 00:12:53,106
Stay quiet, man.

272
00:12:54,874 --> 00:12:57,277
Hey, kid.
Your father at home?

273
00:12:57,277 --> 00:13:01,547
- I don't have a father.
- Oh. Does the harbormaster
live here?

274
00:13:01,547 --> 00:13:03,783
It's the right place
you've come to, then. Come in.

275
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:06,753
Did you see me in
"how green was my valley"?

276
00:13:09,889 --> 00:13:13,092
Me mum's at work, so I'm havin'
a garage sale with her stuff.

277
00:13:13,092 --> 00:13:15,495
You say the harbormaster
lives here?

278
00:13:15,495 --> 00:13:19,399
Yes. But there's a city man
here. A government man.

279
00:13:19,399 --> 00:13:21,601
- WHO IS HE? WHAT'S HE DO?
- McCARTIN'S HIS NAME.

280
00:13:21,601 --> 00:13:24,437
Calls himself an, uh--
oculist.

281
00:13:24,437 --> 00:13:28,174
- What's your name?
- Sean. I work for him.

282
00:13:28,174 --> 00:13:32,245
- Doing what?
- Well, a bit of this,
and a bit of that.

283
00:13:32,245 --> 00:13:34,747
Pinning up the things he finds.

284
00:13:34,747 --> 00:13:37,583
- What things?
- Want to see them, then?

285
00:13:37,583 --> 00:13:38,918
Yeah, sure.

286
00:13:38,918 --> 00:13:41,454
You know, he looks like
a chimp that's dressed up.

287
00:13:43,389 --> 00:13:44,691
♪ Doo, doo-doo ♪

288
00:13:50,897 --> 00:13:54,167
Hey, look over there: It's an
ancient celtic waffle iron.

289
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:56,302
Cool.

290
00:13:56,302 --> 00:13:59,806
Uh, kid, how does this huge room
fit into this tiny little hut?

291
00:14:02,241 --> 00:14:04,243
♪♪ [Whistles]
Well, what do you know?

292
00:14:04,243 --> 00:14:06,179
[All together]
"Not much, you?"

293
00:14:09,349 --> 00:14:12,051
That's been under the sea
a thousand years, they say.

294
00:14:12,051 --> 00:14:13,986
- Hmm?
- Viking, looks like.

295
00:14:13,986 --> 00:14:16,255
- Yeah?
- That's it.

296
00:14:16,255 --> 00:14:18,491
It was a great sea battle,
right off the bay here.

297
00:14:18,491 --> 00:14:21,561
- That's g-r-reat.
- And rory drove them off,
and sank their ships.

298
00:14:21,561 --> 00:14:24,931
- What's that?
- Oh, that's a duck we gave
bovine growth hormone.

299
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:30,503
That's elgra, the sea spirit.

300
00:14:30,503 --> 00:14:33,339
Fine work he did that day.

301
00:14:33,339 --> 00:14:35,608
Sounds like st. patrick
and the snakes.

302
00:14:35,608 --> 00:14:37,543
What are you doing here?

303
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:39,479
- You get out.
- Samuel beckett!

304
00:14:41,414 --> 00:14:44,183
I'm joe ryan.
That's my partner, sam slade.

305
00:14:44,183 --> 00:14:47,186
- HI.
- McCARTIN'S THE NAME.

306
00:14:47,186 --> 00:14:49,889
- Salvage vessel, aren't you?
- Yeah.

307
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:51,791
I thought so.

308
00:14:51,791 --> 00:14:53,626
Did the boy tell you
about all this?

309
00:14:53,626 --> 00:14:56,529
- Yeah, a little.
- This stuff has no real value.

310
00:14:56,529 --> 00:14:59,432
Except to us eggheads.
But since it turned up,

311
00:14:59,432 --> 00:15:01,067
no ships allowed
at nyda island

312
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:03,035
for more than 24 hours
without a permit.

313
00:15:03,035 --> 00:15:05,838
Look, friend,
we're not seaworthy.

314
00:15:05,838 --> 00:15:07,607
We won't be
for three or four days.

315
00:15:07,607 --> 00:15:11,344
I don't make the law.
That's the way it is.

316
00:15:11,344 --> 00:15:13,646
Anyway, we're afloat.
Come on, sam.

317
00:15:13,646 --> 00:15:16,883
We'll go find
a better harbor master.

318
00:15:16,883 --> 00:15:20,086
- How about fresh water?
- We'll give you that.

319
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:22,121
- Thanks.
- No hard feelings, now.

320
00:15:22,121 --> 00:15:25,224
- Oh, no.
- Now, wait. You guys,
I think there might be.

321
00:15:25,224 --> 00:15:27,160
Please, let's talk this out!

322
00:15:29,428 --> 00:15:31,798
You believe him,
about those permits?

323
00:15:33,032 --> 00:15:35,301
- No.
- Well, something's eating him.

324
00:15:35,301 --> 00:15:38,004
- You mean, besides the lice?
- I wonder what.

325
00:15:39,105 --> 00:15:41,274
I don't know.

326
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:44,677
Come on. Maybe we'll swing
a little more weight around here

327
00:15:44,677 --> 00:15:47,680
- if we find out.
- But let's get some
boiled cabbage first.

328
00:15:50,416 --> 00:15:52,885
Ah, it's the yearly
selkie clubbin'.

329
00:15:54,821 --> 00:15:56,556
Hey, joe, look!

330
00:15:56,556 --> 00:15:59,292
He's new to sailoring, and he's
still pointing out boats.

331
00:16:02,862 --> 00:16:05,531
- Back 'er off, harry.
- I beg your pardon?

332
00:16:06,666 --> 00:16:09,368
Oh, we're a terrible crew team.

333
00:16:10,469 --> 00:16:12,171
Are you having any luck?

334
00:16:12,171 --> 00:16:14,807
- I've got some [foreign word].
- Hmm! Wow.

335
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:17,877
You know, joe, they can
talk english every bit
as good as you or I can.

336
00:16:17,877 --> 00:16:19,378
They just don't want to,
that's all.

337
00:16:19,378 --> 00:16:22,982
- You try 'em, harry.
- [Speaking foreign language]

338
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:25,585
You have a good time
to hear of necessity.

339
00:16:25,585 --> 00:16:27,220
WHEN McCARTIN'S ABOUT.

340
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:29,121
He said there's no time
for talkin' with strangers,

341
00:16:29,121 --> 00:16:31,123
AND McCARTIN DOES ALL
THE TALKING ON THE ISLAND.

342
00:16:31,123 --> 00:16:33,659
Well, he said, "blow it out
your--" something, I'm not sure.

343
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:39,298
Joe strummer goes fishing.

344
00:16:39,298 --> 00:16:42,935
- [Foreign word]
- You have a great tide
to your necessity.

345
00:16:42,935 --> 00:16:44,804
Two of the divers
didn't come up, joe.

346
00:16:44,804 --> 00:16:47,306
- They think they're gone.
- Gone?

347
00:16:47,306 --> 00:16:49,242
[Crow] Yes, a word meaning,
"not here anymore."

348
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:55,014
[Servo] Stop shaking the boat.
I'm gonna puke.

349
00:16:56,983 --> 00:16:59,752
[Imitates foreign language]

350
00:16:59,752 --> 00:17:01,220
There's one!

351
00:17:02,488 --> 00:17:04,690
Colin's here.
[Foreign language]

352
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:07,159
He's got two time-release
caplets on his back.

353
00:17:07,159 --> 00:17:09,862
- Well, now he's only got one!
- Hey!

354
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:12,798
Aye.

355
00:17:12,798 --> 00:17:17,036
"Overcome by an excess of
potatoes, guinness and guilt."

356
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:19,972
- [Coughing]
- Okay, let's take a look
of that butt.

357
00:17:25,745 --> 00:17:27,013
SO THAT'S WHAT'S
WORRYING McCARTIN.

358
00:17:28,681 --> 00:17:30,816
I should visit tennille
when I'm ashore.

359
00:17:32,818 --> 00:17:35,021
The mackerel's in the-- ugh.

360
00:17:38,024 --> 00:17:40,493
- He's dead.
- Dead? How?

361
00:17:40,493 --> 00:17:43,062
- How dead? Well, just dead!
- You saw him come up.

362
00:17:44,797 --> 00:17:47,033
If you ask me,
he died of fright.

363
00:17:47,033 --> 00:17:49,602
Couldn't be the boiled back fat
he ate every day of his life!

364
00:17:53,439 --> 00:17:56,542
I think that's our ship, it's
just they all look the same.

365
00:17:58,344 --> 00:18:00,513
- This is crazy--
- us, marrying.

366
00:18:00,513 --> 00:18:03,616
There was a man lost down there
today, not even a trace.

367
00:18:03,616 --> 00:18:06,886
Another one saw something
that scared him to death.

368
00:18:06,886 --> 00:18:09,789
Look, sam. You don't
want to go, don't go.

369
00:18:09,789 --> 00:18:13,526
I'm going all right. Just to
make sure that you get back.

370
00:18:13,526 --> 00:18:17,363
- Ooh, I got back.
- Sure. With a hatful of gold.

371
00:18:17,363 --> 00:18:20,433
- Ha? You get it?
- Get set.

372
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:23,769
- Yeah, okay.
- How do these things work?

373
00:18:28,307 --> 00:18:30,242
Well, this one
smells like yours.

374
00:18:35,414 --> 00:18:37,984
- A boat made of
foot-long hot dogs.
- [Giggles]

375
00:18:40,186 --> 00:18:42,722
Now, I'm just gonna hang it out
over the side here. Don't look.

376
00:18:48,260 --> 00:18:51,430
- "Thunderbore!"
- "voyage to the bottom
of the yawn!"

377
00:18:51,430 --> 00:18:55,001
- "The abys-mal."
- "Driving miss dummy."

378
00:18:55,001 --> 00:18:57,269
[Mike] Wait. Th-that really
doesn't work at all.

379
00:18:57,269 --> 00:19:00,473
- Really?
- No. Really fails
on a whole lot of levels.

380
00:19:00,473 --> 00:19:04,610
- Well, I try, mike, right?
- [Whispers] Sorry.

381
00:19:04,610 --> 00:19:07,680
Watch for sharks.
I accidentally bathed
in fish blood this morning.

382
00:19:16,522 --> 00:19:18,824
Did you say
"bl-ub, bl-bl-blub"?

383
00:19:23,629 --> 00:19:26,832
Well, all this hard water.
Ireland needs the culligan man.

384
00:19:28,934 --> 00:19:31,037
Counting plankton
is really hard.

385
00:19:36,709 --> 00:19:39,645
Ooh. Somebody sunk a macy's
thanksgiving day parade balloon.

386
00:19:42,682 --> 00:19:44,850
Come on, let's get some
stale bread and feed it.

387
00:19:46,652 --> 00:19:48,521
You know what's
great though, sam?

388
00:19:48,521 --> 00:19:51,590
I'm wetting my pants entire,
but it really doesn't matter
down here.

389
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:58,998
- What did you see, sam?
- You borrowed
my old dish towel?

390
00:19:58,998 --> 00:20:01,033
I don't know.

391
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:03,369
But whatever it was, I never
want to see it again.

392
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:06,272
Oh, like you're this big prize.
[Chuckles]

393
00:20:10,009 --> 00:20:13,779
[Irish accent]
♪ show me the way to go home ♪

394
00:20:13,779 --> 00:20:15,448
♪ tired and I wa... ♪

395
00:20:15,448 --> 00:20:17,149
There's a dead hobbit
in that tube.

396
00:20:20,086 --> 00:20:22,088
How goes it, sam?

397
00:20:22,088 --> 00:20:24,156
These are the last few barrels
coming on board now.

398
00:20:24,156 --> 00:20:27,026
Well, clear the stage for
a campy musical review.

399
00:20:28,194 --> 00:20:30,362
Oh, keep back.

400
00:20:30,362 --> 00:20:33,032
- CAPTAIN WANTS TO SEE YA.
- THOUGHT HIS NAME
WAS McBOX.

401
00:20:33,032 --> 00:20:36,202
- A fine rage he's in.
- Oh, it is, is it?

402
00:20:36,202 --> 00:20:37,736
[Imitating a chimp]

403
00:20:38,938 --> 00:20:40,973
Look, kid. Get down
off there, will ya?

404
00:20:40,973 --> 00:20:43,442
- About the permit.
- What about the permit?

405
00:20:43,442 --> 00:20:45,277
It's a heathen lie.

406
00:20:45,277 --> 00:20:48,280
Maybe we'd better see
what this joker's got
in mind. Where is he?

407
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:51,083
- Come on, then.
- All right.

408
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:53,619
Well, here's the script.
You take my part in the movie
for a while.

409
00:20:57,923 --> 00:21:01,060
Their polynesian torch ceremony
isn't too successful this year.

410
00:21:02,895 --> 00:21:05,798
- What's going on here?
- They think a shark got
the man who was lost.

411
00:21:10,803 --> 00:21:14,273
♪ Bali hai will call you ♪

412
00:21:19,245 --> 00:21:21,580
MR. McCARTIN, I HEAR
YOU'VE GOT A BEEF.

413
00:21:21,580 --> 00:21:23,616
You were snoopin' around
out there.

414
00:21:23,616 --> 00:21:25,417
My diver was tellin' me.

415
00:21:25,417 --> 00:21:28,621
Yeah, and I suppose
they told you to give us
all that jazz about a permit.

416
00:21:28,621 --> 00:21:30,456
Are you doubtin' my word?

417
00:21:30,456 --> 00:21:32,324
YOU'RE RIGHT, MR. McCARTIN,
I AM.

418
00:21:32,324 --> 00:21:34,727
Look, I'm trying to write
krapp's last tape.

419
00:21:37,530 --> 00:21:40,499
May your corned beef
not pickle correctly.

420
00:21:40,499 --> 00:21:43,035
After you've loaded water,
you leave.

421
00:21:43,035 --> 00:21:45,738
- Tonight.
- The sooner, the better.

422
00:21:45,738 --> 00:21:48,073
The tighter the sweater,
the boys depend on us.

423
00:21:48,073 --> 00:21:52,545
Say, there's like one cod
left in the north atlantic,

424
00:21:52,545 --> 00:21:54,880
but damn it, they're
gonna get it!

425
00:21:56,282 --> 00:21:57,249
[Guffawing]

426
00:22:00,519 --> 00:22:02,121
[Speaking gaelic]

427
00:22:02,121 --> 00:22:03,956
That was just grandma
takin' a swim-- don't!

428
00:22:10,496 --> 00:22:12,731
- Oh. Ow!
- [Laughing]

429
00:22:13,799 --> 00:22:15,734
- Wow.
- [Trumpeting]

430
00:22:15,734 --> 00:22:17,870
Patty-cake, patty-cake...

431
00:22:19,438 --> 00:22:21,173
Go check that out, kid.

432
00:22:22,641 --> 00:22:25,110
- [Roaring]
- Dorkin!

433
00:22:25,110 --> 00:22:27,179
How are ya?

434
00:22:29,281 --> 00:22:31,917
It's the rare isosceles-eared
underwater dragon!

435
00:22:34,086 --> 00:22:37,189
Really, gentlemen,
must we do this every night?

436
00:22:39,158 --> 00:22:41,193
Oh, poor robert shaw.
Eaten again.

437
00:22:46,131 --> 00:22:48,500
♪ To reach ♪

438
00:23:04,617 --> 00:23:07,519
Oh, hello. I'm diana rigg.

439
00:23:07,519 --> 00:23:09,855
Inspired by the guy
in today's movie,

440
00:23:09,855 --> 00:23:12,424
who looks kind of like
samuel beckett,

441
00:23:12,424 --> 00:23:15,861
we present to you a tragic
comedy, in one act.

442
00:23:15,861 --> 00:23:18,130
Waiting for gorgo.

443
00:23:18,130 --> 00:23:19,765
Thank you, won't we?

444
00:23:28,073 --> 00:23:30,542
Nothing to be done.

445
00:23:30,542 --> 00:23:33,178
I'm beginning to come 'round
to that opinion.

446
00:23:35,381 --> 00:23:37,983
- Let's go.
- We can't.

447
00:23:37,983 --> 00:23:41,887
- Why not?
- We're... waiting for gorgo.

448
00:23:41,887 --> 00:23:44,323
- Ah, yeah.
- Rowr-ah-rowr!

449
00:23:44,323 --> 00:23:47,993
Ah! And there he is!
Oh-ho, stop!

450
00:23:47,993 --> 00:23:50,129
Aah! No! No! No!

451
00:23:50,129 --> 00:23:51,930
- [Roaring]
- Mother! Ow...

452
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:54,133
- [Crashing]
- [Roars]

453
00:23:56,935 --> 00:23:58,971
[Clapping]

454
00:23:58,971 --> 00:24:00,906
[Cheering]

455
00:24:05,344 --> 00:24:07,279
Ah, thank you.

456
00:24:08,814 --> 00:24:11,016
[Laughing]

457
00:24:11,016 --> 00:24:13,152
[Cheering continues]

458
00:24:17,122 --> 00:24:19,692
[Louder cheering]

459
00:24:27,900 --> 00:24:30,402
[Rhythmic clapping]

460
00:24:45,918 --> 00:24:48,420
No more, please.
[Chuckling]

461
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:50,222
Oh, my.

462
00:24:54,326 --> 00:24:56,261
We'll be back
after this message

463
00:24:56,261 --> 00:24:58,330
from whiskey and cigarettes.

464
00:25:07,639 --> 00:25:10,642
- Ah, nice one.
- Must be cigarettes.

465
00:25:10,642 --> 00:25:12,578
Look at this. The poor irish,
you know?

466
00:25:12,578 --> 00:25:14,179
If they're not
invaded by cromwell,

467
00:25:14,179 --> 00:25:16,849
or infested with leprechauns,
they got this guy!

468
00:25:20,285 --> 00:25:21,820
[Imitating boy]
I've got me slingshot.

469
00:25:21,820 --> 00:25:23,122
Shoot!

470
00:25:24,390 --> 00:25:25,691
No, no!

471
00:25:25,691 --> 00:25:28,260
♪ Shuffle off to buff-a-lo ♪

472
00:25:30,429 --> 00:25:33,499
- [GROWLING]
- McROAR! O'GROWL!

473
00:25:35,768 --> 00:25:38,737
Sorry, I'm a little-- can you
tell me how to get to tokyo?

474
00:25:42,808 --> 00:25:44,176
Quick, let's emigrate.

475
00:25:50,115 --> 00:25:51,650
- No. No!
- Let go!

476
00:25:51,650 --> 00:25:53,419
Guy's good at
pushing kids around.

477
00:26:00,159 --> 00:26:01,994
Mm, habanero sauce.

478
00:26:04,296 --> 00:26:06,131
Not a very good juggling act.

479
00:26:08,333 --> 00:26:11,904
Ah, real shame for the island.
The let's go europe people
are visiting tonight.

480
00:26:11,904 --> 00:26:13,605
Aw.

